==History==
===Entrance Into Apex with MajorPushers (2023)===
Aurora Gaming made their entrance into Apex Legends by signing the [[MajorPushers]] roster ahead of the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2022/Split_1/Pro_League/EMEA|first Split]] of the third ALGS year. Acquiring the lineup consisting of Kirill "[[RANCHES]]" Rulin, Denis "[[cleaveee]]" Rassokhin, and Alexey "[[Maliwan]]" Rusinov, a team that was also previously a part of the Russian organization [[Team Empire]]. <ref name="Aurora enters"/> The team had already seen great successes under Empire, having won the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2022/Split_2/Pro_League/EMEA|second split of EMEA 2022]] and finishing in eighth at the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2022/Split_2/Playoffs|Split 2 Playoffs]] in Stockholm, Sweden. Despite the team not being able to attend the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2022/Championship|2022 Championship]] due to visa issues <ref name="emp withdrew">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/Ranchesje/status/1541315764929568770|title=we miss the championship, visa denial to all three|author=[[RANCHES]]|date=2022-06-27|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> and later parting ways with [[Team Empire]] <ref name="Empire disbands">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/team_empire/status/1556686731453370370|title=Today we’re leaving competitive Apex Legends and announce the departure from our Apex ex-squad.|author=[[Team Empire]]|date=2022-08-08|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>, they were still looking to continue on their successes from the previous year.

During the regular season, Aurora had a consistent season, securing a win on one of the matchdays they found themselves in an eventual race for first place against [[Acend]]. With the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2022/Split_1/Pro_League/EMEA/Final|Finals week]], they were then able to secure a second-place finish, acquiring five more points than Acend to push themselves into first. Securing themselves the first seed out of the EMEA region for the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Split_1/Playoffs|2023 Split 1 Playoffs]]. However, disaster struck once again for the team as the three players were unable to acquire their visas in time for the event leading them to be replaced by [[Horizon Union]]. <ref name="Aurora disqualified">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/cleaveeje/status/1621065573349171201|title=With a heavy heart we must announce that our team "Aurora" will not be able to participate in the ALGS Split 1 Playoffs in London|author=[[cleaveee]]|date=2023-02-02|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

The following [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Split_2/Playoffs|Split]] however started off rough as the team started the first matchdays with a performance below expectations.  This led the team to bench Maliwan and Aurora signed Danila "[[Sunset]]" Soloviov in his place. <ref name="Maliwan inactive"/><ref name="Sunset joins"/> Although the team's performance didn't rise drastically with the change, Aurora was able to increase their placement on matchdays, and with a sixth-place finish in the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Split_2/Pro_League/EMEA/Final|Finals]] and teams like [[Horizon Union]] and [[start a fight Esports]] having a bad performance they were able to clinch a 9th place in the overall standings, securing themselves a spot at the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Split_2/Playoffs|Split 2 Playoffs]].

With the visas from the first split that they were able to eventually acquire which lasted long enough for the second LAN the team also was for the most part able to attend the event. However, as Sunset wasn't a part of the team in the prior split he still had to go through the process of acquiring one. Sunset was then unable to acquire a visa in time for the event to start so the team had to bring back Maliwan who still had his. <ref name="Maliwan standin">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/cleaveeje/status/1679425267842928640|title=Today is the day we all have been waiting for so long!|author=[[cleaveee]]|date=2023-07-13|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> However together with Maliwan they still had to face [[DarkZero Esports]] in a contest for Harvest on [[World's Edge]] during the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Split_2/Playoffs/Group_Stage|group stages]]. Making matters worse is that they also shared their group with the Australian team, meaning they had to deal with the contest in all of the group-stage matches. Although Aurora made a strong start in the contest in their first set, DarkZero turned their strategy around for the following rounds, beating Aurora convincingly, and also looked to contest them on [[Storm Point]] to ensure that Aurora would finish outside of the top 20, sending them to the losers bracket. Following the conclusion of the group stages though, Sunset was able to acquire his visa and made it to the LAN for the bracket stage. <ref name="Sunset makes it">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TheAurora_GG/status/1680141082846265345|title=The Boys are back!|author='''Aurora Gaming'''|date=2023-07-16|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> Despite now being a full squad though, the team fell just short of advancing in the losers bracket, as they narrowly missed out of the top ten by a single point, finishing in eleventh behind [[Riddle]].

Following the Playoffs, Aurora parted ways with the roster, but it would not be long before their return to Apex Legends. <ref name="Aurora disbands"/> 

{{Quote |quote = "For almost a year now, our team has been an integral part of every big Apex Legends tournament. We have won many times, became the best team in the EU, qualified for LAN tournaments and failed at Last Chance Qualifications - a long story. This is where our paths with the guys diverge. We thank them very much for everything they have done for our organization and of course we don't forget the fans who have been following this roster since its inception. It's been a long road, but it's time to move on."|sign =Aurora Gaming|source = <ref name="Aurora disbands"/>  }}

===Acquiring the Fire Beavers (2023)===
Twenty days later after parting with their original roster, Aurora announced their acquisition of the [[Fire Beavers]]. <ref name="FB join"/> Bringing in Kiryl "[[9impulse]]" Kostsiu, Svyatoslav "[[ojrein]]" Korochinsky, Lev "[[taskmast33r]]" Grigoriev, and their coach Nikita "[[clawz]]" Marchinsky. The team which had a similar route as Aurora beforehand as they had also missed out on the first playoffs. However, with Fire Beavers making the finals off the second playoffs, they had secured their spot for the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Championship|2023 Championship]] in Birmingham.

The team however once again was facing visa issues coming into the event as they were still awaiting a response days before the event. Eventually ojrein was the first player to confirm his visa just two days before the tournament started. <ref name="oj visa">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ojrein/status/1698680114802737218|title=Got my visa, god blessed! Cya at lan|author=[[ojrein]]|date=2023-09-04|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> With ojrein confirmed the team was at the very least able to keep their spot as they were allowed to bring in two emergency substitutes. Bringing along Jose "[[Uxako]]" Llosa and Keenan "[[Tax]]" Mackey. <ref name="subs">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/AuroraApex_GG/status/1699027186567500149|title=Due to visa issues, we had to invite substitutes to participate in the Champs. Thanks to @Taxington and @UxakoTTV for help.|author=Aurora Gaming|date=2023-09-05|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> Following their announcement of their two substitutes, it was also confirmed that 9impulse had acquired his visa and made it to the event in time for the first day, meaning they opted to play with Uxako as their third. <ref name="9imps arrives">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/AuroraApex_GG/status/1699205020044976505|title=Boss has arrived|author=Aurora Gaming|date=2023-09-06|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> 

Starting the first day of the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2023/Championship/Group_Stage|Group Stage]] Aurora had a decent performance in their first group ending in tenth, but failed to make an impact in their second group, finishing 16th. Following the disappointing performance the team initially looked to make a change as they felt it wasn't clicking with Uxako due to legend selection and communication issues. <ref name="uxako tax issues">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/UxakoTTV/status/1700103271556210695|title=After those rough days, Aurora decided to play with Tax (their emergency sub).|author=[[Uxako]]|date=2023-09-08|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref><ref name="uxako tax issues2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/9Impu1se/status/1700246100966248816|title=Guys uxako travelled not for his own, everything was paid for him,|author=[[Aurora Gaming]]|date=2023-09-08|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> Instead, the team wanted to try to continue with Tax. However, since Tax was signed up as the emergency substitute and the situation regarding the roster swapped wasn't deemed an emergency situation they were unable to make the substitution. <ref name="ruling">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TheeTabris/status/1700109675444809827|title=So this means Aurora is choosing to play with 2 players. A qualifying emergency would have to occur to allow them to utilize an emergency sub.|author=Zac Conely|date=2023-09-08|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> After the rule was clarified, Uxako refused to continue after the fact, leaving 9impulse and ojrein to finish the tournament as a duo. Although the two continued to play out the tournament, they eventually were eliminated in 16th in the first losers bracket round.

===Adding the Grim Griefer (2024)===
Ahead of the fourth year of the ALGS, Aurora made the move to bench taskmast33r. <ref name="task inactive"/> In his place, they signed Konstantin "[[Hardecki]]" Kozlov. <ref name="Hardecki joins"/>Although his latest stint under the [[Gaimin Gladiators]] left much to be desired, Hardecki was still seen as a strong player who had earned himself the nickname of the "The Grim Griefer" over his years of playing. <ref name="GrimGriefer">{{cite web|url=https://esports.gg/guides/apex-legends/five-years-of-apex-the-best-algs-clutches-of-all-time/|title=Hardecki makes T-Rex extinct|author=[[Tom Bull]] |date=2024-02-04|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> And with this move, it seemed the team was looking to push themselves to new heights. As in the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2024/Split_1/Pro_League/EMEA|First Split]] of the EMEA Pro League Aurora made a dominant splash, securing themselves three victories and a second place across four group stage series'. They had already secured their spot at the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2024/Split_1/Playoffs|2024 Playoffs Split 1]] while still having 2 matchdays and a final ahead of them. Following another victory and another 15 points on the last regular season day, they also set themselves up to earn the most points in a split. On which they delivered as they also managed to win the finals, smashing the record previously set by [[Moist Esports]] (A 151 points), as they ended the split on a 161 points.

